    "description": "This lovely remodeled 1904 Victorian flat is located at San Francisco's charming \"Inner Sunset\" neighborhood, conveniently located in the heart of the city. It's surrounded with dozens of world cuisine restaurants and coffee shops, Sunday Farmers Market and offers many other daily conveniences.\n\nA half block away is the famous Golden Gate Park where you can walk to its many great attractions. The N-Judah street car line is just steps from your door for traveling downtown with ease. And Ocean Beach is just five minutes away.\nThis 2-unit building was completely remodeled. Quiet, nice professionals live above. All new electrical and plumbing, appliances, water heater and furnace with forced air and central heating. This is a rare opportunity to live in a beautiful, tastefully renovated owners unit. \n\n Entire first floor private flat\n 975 sq. ft. of living area\n 1 bedroom + 2 rooms\n 1 full bath with lovely spa decor\n Modern kitchen with gas stove, refrigerator, microwave, garbage disposal, hot/cold filtered water\n Large, sunny, peaceful back yard with room for a BBQ and garden\n Hard-wired Gig network in every room\n High original Victorian ceilings, new paint\n Spacious front room with bay windows overlooking 9th Ave.\n Lots of natural light\n Beautiful new hardwood floors throughout\n Small, sunny wood deck in back\n Washer and dryer on site (included)\n \n* Garage parking spot available (rented separately)\n* Storage space in garage (rented separately)\n\nOne of SF's best neighborhoods:\n\n 30+ restaurants, coffee shops, banks, boutiques, post office, etc. at your front steps!\n Perfect for UCSF employees walk to work\n 1/2 block from the Golden Gate Park's main entrance enjoy the DeYoung Museum, Academy of Science, Japanese Tea Garden, Botanical Flower Gardens, jogging, biking trails and more!\n Steps from public transportation, N-Judah and Express Muni to downtown in minutes\n 3 blocks from super-market, 1/2 block from mini-market and Starbucks\n 2 minute drive to SF's second Chinatown 23rd and Irving\n 5 minute drive to Ocean Beach, Cliff House, Beach Chalet, Lands End hiking trails\n Very friendly neighborhood, great for families and kids\n\n1 year lease, month to month thereafter\n 1 month security deposit\n No smokers or pets\n Application fee: $45 for credit check"
  },
